### Calendar API – try the endpoints from VS / VS Code / Rider.
### Run the API first (dotnet run --project src/CalendarApi), then send requests top to bottom.
### Requests capture IDs from earlier responses, so run them in order.

@host = http://localhost:5063

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Calendars

### Create a calendar for alice
# @name createWork
POST {{host}}/api/calendars
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerId": "alice", "name": "Work", "description": "Work events" }

###
@workId = {{createWork.response.body.$.id}}

### A user can own many calendars
# @name createPersonal
POST {{host}}/api/calendars
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ownerId": "alice", "name": "Personal" }

### List all calendars
GET {{host}}/api/calendars

### List only alice's calendars
GET {{host}}/api/calendars?ownerId=alice

### Get one calendar
GET {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}

### Rename a calendar (owner cannot change)
PUT {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Work (renamed)", "description": "Updated" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Resources (meeting rooms)

### Create a room
# @name createRoom
POST {{host}}/api/resources
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Boardroom", "description": "3rd floor", "capacity": 10 }

###
@roomId = {{createRoom.response.body.$.id}}

### List rooms
GET {{host}}/api/resources

### Get one room
GET {{host}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}

### Update a room
PUT {{host}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Boardroom", "description": "3rd floor, projector", "capacity": 12 }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Events

### One-off event, booking the room
# @name createOneOff
POST {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Planning",
  "start": "2026-01-06T13:00:00Z",
  "end": "2026-01-06T14:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{roomId}}"
}

###
@oneOffId = {{createOneOff.response.body.$.id}}

### Daily stand-up for 5 days (no room)
POST {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Daily sync",
  "start": "2026-01-05T08:30:00Z",
  "end": "2026-01-05T08:45:00Z",
  "recurrence": { "frequency": "Daily", "count": 5 }
}

### Weekly Mon/Wed/Fri stand-up in the room, every week, until 31 March
# @name createWeekly
POST {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Stand-up",
  "start": "2026-01-05T09:00:00Z",
  "end": "2026-01-05T09:30:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{roomId}}",
  "recurrence": {
    "frequency": "Weekly",
    "interval": 1,
    "daysOfWeek": ["Monday", "Wednesday", "Friday"],
    "until": "2026-03-31T00:00:00Z"
  }
}

###
@weeklyId = {{createWeekly.response.body.$.id}}

### List stored events (a series appears once)
GET {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events

### Get one event
GET {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events/{{weeklyId}}

### Update an event (replaces the whole series): move the one-off
PUT {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events/{{oneOffId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Planning (moved)",
  "start": "2026-01-06T15:00:00Z",
  "end": "2026-01-06T16:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{roomId}}"
}

### Expanded occurrences for a window (recurring events unfolded)
GET {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/occurrences?from=2026-01-05T00:00:00Z&to=2026-01-19T00:00:00Z

### All bookings of the room, across every calendar
GET {{host}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}/occurrences?from=2026-01-05T00:00:00Z&to=2026-01-19T00:00:00Z

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Error cases

### 409: double-booking the room (clashes with the Monday stand-up)
POST {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Clash",
  "start": "2026-01-12T09:15:00Z",
  "end": "2026-01-12T10:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{roomId}}"
}

### 400: validation (blank title, end before start)
POST {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "start": "2026-01-05T10:00:00Z", "end": "2026-01-05T09:00:00Z" }

### 409: cannot delete a room that still has bookings
DELETE {{host}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- Cleanup

### Delete the whole series
DELETE {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events/{{weeklyId}}

### Delete an event
DELETE {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}/events/{{oneOffId}}

### Delete the room (allowed now that no events book it)
DELETE {{host}}/api/resources/{{roomId}}

### Delete the calendar (also deletes its events)
DELETE {{host}}/api/calendars/{{workId}}
